---
id: org.dxos.review.composer-plugins
name: ComposerPluginRules
version: 0.1.0
---

Review rules promoted from `.agents/skills/composer-plugins/MEMORY.md` — recurring
session-logged corrections that are mechanically checkable. When a MEMORY.md bullet
stabilizes into a pattern a subagent can verify, it belongs here so the agentic-review
harness enforces it on every run.

## Extensions

| Term   | URI                   |
| ------ | --------------------- |
| `rule` | org.dxos.mdl.rule@1.0 |

## Rules

```mdl
rule no-capability-hooks-in-components: Components must not call capability hooks
  Files under a plugin's `src/components/` must not call capability hooks —
  `useCapability`, `useCapabilities`, `useAppGraph`, `useOperationInvoker`, or
  `useProcessManagerRuntime`. All of them throw without a `PluginManager`, which
  makes the component unmountable in storybook. Resolve the capability once in
  the container (under `src/containers/`) and thread the resolved value down as
  a prop or via the composite's `Root` context; per-item helper hooks take the
  resolved value as a parameter. Do not flag files under `src/containers/` or
  hooks that merely receive an already-resolved invoker/runtime as an argument.
  Known pre-existing violations exist in plugin-inbox; still flag them.
  scope: repo
  files:
    - packages/plugins/**/src/components/**/*.ts
    - packages/plugins/**/src/components/**/*.tsx
  grep: useCapability|useCapabilities|useAppGraph|useOperationInvoker|useProcessManagerRuntime
  severity: warn
```
